    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0021" n="5" xml:id="pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.50/2–1948</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director, Office of Financial and
                        Development Policy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Ness</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Secretary of State for Economic Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Thorp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-02-19">February 19, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At the January 14 meeting of the Policy Committee of the Bogotá Conference, Mr.
                        Armour<anchor n="1" xml:id="d3-f1"/> suggested that a statement from OFD on an affirmative economic program and policy
                    of assistance to Latin America would be desirable.</p>
                <p>Attached is a statement setting forth in general terms what might be the
                    principal elements of such a program.</p>


                <xi:include href="d3-a1.xml" xpointer="d3-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
